\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Strong yen offers scant solace. \b0\par\par\uc2 830 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 1999\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0915 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly weak in \par \par \uc2  late trade as the dollar regained its footing above 109 yen, \par \par \uc2  with the market lacking energy to push it beyond its day low \par \par \uc2  around 108.70. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the dollar's trend was clearly bearish, but it \par \par \uc2  needed some correction before heading lower against the yen. \par \par \uc2      The market was also wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though a series of warnings by officials failed to spur \par \par \uc2  active yen sales. \par \par \uc2      Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi \par \par \uc2  reiterated on Thursday that Japan was ready to act to curb a \par \par \uc2  rapid, premature rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht remained downcast, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  saying it had no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite its drop to \par \par \uc2  11-month lows on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul attributed the \par \par \uc2  baht's weakness to market speculation of possible political \par \par \uc2  changes in Thailand and a perception it was making slow \par \par \uc2  progress in restructuring corporate debt. \par \par \uc2      "Key Thai economic indicators remain sound and NPL \par \par \uc2  restructuring may be sluggish but it will improve," he said. \par \par \uc2      Earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the baht's setback had been \par \par \uc2  accelerated by Thai-based Japanese companies repatriating \par \par \uc2  dollars and a concurrent decision by many Thai exporters to \par \par \uc2  delay selling dollar holdings until the baht stabilised. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht had come under pressure from \par \par \uc2  corporate dollar demand and rumours a U.S-based hedge fund was \par \par \uc2  targeting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Most dealers and analysts dismissed talk of a speculative \par \par \uc2  attack, but said the baht was being hurt by foreign investor \par \par \uc2  concerns about Thailand's troubled financial sector. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah was pressured but managed to steer clear of \par \par \uc2  the 7,800 level, seen as a trigger-point to further weakness, \par \par \uc2  amid worries about mounting violence in East Timor. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta's top military spokesman said it would be logical \par \par \uc2  for Indonesia to allow a U.N. force to go to East Timor if the \par \par \uc2  result of Monday's referendum turned out to be strongly in \par \par \uc2  favour of independence. \par \par \uc2  At least five people were killed on Wednesday in clashes \par \par \uc2  outside the U.N. headquarters in Dili, prompting calls for a \par \par \uc2  U.N. peacekeeping force and condemnation of Indonesia's failure \par \par \uc2  to rein in pro-Jakarta militias. \par \par \uc2      Further ripples from the Bank Bali scandal also kept \par \par \uc2  sentiment on the rupiah bearish. \par \par \uc2      Planning Minister Budiono said Indonesia's budget would be \par \par \uc2  affected if the issue was not resolved soon. \par \par \uc2      The World Bank and IMF have threatened to suspend vital \par \par \uc2  financial aid if the case is not settled. \par \par \uc2      *** The won eased amid dollar demand for import settlements \par \par \uc2  and from foreign investors bailing out of local equities amid \par \par \uc2  concerns of a stock manipulation probe of Hyundai Group \par \par \uc2  executives. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said monetary policy for September would \par \par \uc2  focus on stabilising financial markets by keeping the overnight \par \par \uc2  rate low in the wake of the Daewoo Group's troubles. \par \par \uc2      It said inflationary pressure remained subdued despite the \par \par \uc2  faster-than-expected economic recovery. \par \par \uc2      *** The peso slipped as banks shored up their dollar \par \par \uc2  positions amid concerns about the weaker baht. Thailand and the \par \par \uc2  Philippines compete in export markets. \par \par \uc2      The peso was also weighed down by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying \par \par \uc2  it would keep overnight rates and reserve requirements steady \par \par \uc2  as the market has been holding out for higher rates in the wake \par \par \uc2  of last week's U.S. rate hike. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the peso \par \par \uc2  should remain stable and not weaken towards the 40 per dollar \par \par \uc2  level even if inflation turned out to be higher in August. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll on Wednesday forecast inflation in the year \par \par \uc2  to August would be at an average of 6.17 percent, up from the \par \par \uc2  5.7 percent annual rise seen in both June and July. \par \par \uc2  Inflation predictions have risen due to floods last month \par \par \uc2  which devestated crops in and around Manila and higher fuel \par \par \uc2  prices. The number is due to be released on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day THU 02 0915GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......