\par\par \b \uc2  IMF Neiss/Japan -2: Remarks Show Intl Concern About Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1999\par 06:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--In the clearest signal yet that the international community is growing more concerned about the strong yen, a senior International Monetary Fund official warned Wednesday that a rapid appreciation of the yen could derail Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  Hubert Neiss, director of the International Monetary Fund's Asia and Pacific department, said in a speech in Tokyo that "a further rapid appreciation of the yen could well put an end to the recovery, as has happened before." \par \par \uc2  "This is an important risk," Neiss said. \par \par \uc2  Neiss urged the Japanese government to take steps to counter the rise of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to ensure that fiscal policy doesn't start to work as a drag on economic growth. Significantly, Neiss included in his remarks specific policy steps that Tokyo could use to prevent the yen from rising. \par \par \uc2  He said that among the macro policy instruments available to fight the strong yen "is mainly a more aggressive monetary policy, which means strong liquidity injections by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "more effective if it is unsterilized because it means an expansionary monetary policy." \par \par \uc2  In unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sell the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and then leave those funds in the money market to create oversupply - and thus easier monetary conditions. In recent months, the Bank of Japan has in fact sopped up extra yen in the money market, thereby undermining the effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to analysts. \par \par \uc2  The remarks by Neiss came against a backdrop of rising concerns in Japan about the dollar's trading level against the yen. Currently, the dollar is quoted around Y109.40 - not far off the low for 1999 of Y108.21 set in early January. \par \par \uc2  As recently as early July, the dollar was trading above Y120. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's slide has spurred notions that Japan and its partners in the Group of Seven might have to resort to coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to break the trend. Thus far, monetary authorities in the other G-7 nations have downplayed the chances of joint action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But Neiss appeared to be gently pressing the case for coordinated action Wednesday. He noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "more effective if done with other central banks." \par \par \uc2  Turning to fiscal policy in Japan, Neiss said there is a risk that "Fiscal policy stimulus put in place last year will taper off and not be offset fully by an additional supplementary budget." \par \par \uc2  Regarding the yen and fiscal policy, he said, "These risks are something the government can do something about." \par \par \uc2  Despite his warnings about the yen and fiscal drag, Neiss said the IMF may upwardly revise its growth forecast for Japan this year. He noted that the IMF now expects Japanese gross domestic product to expand by 0.25% in 1999. \par \par \uc2  This estimate will "probably be raised to one half a percent as things go on," he said. \par \par \uc2  Touching briefly on China's yuan, Neiss said China's government is strong enough to "keep the yuan stable." \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott (813-5255-2929;amscott@ap.org) \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0408GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9106et0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
