\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Limping dollar at 1-week lows vs euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1999\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 1 (Reuters) - The dollar set one-week lows against the euro and was mired near 109 yen on Wednesday, hit by economic evidence suggesting a pick-up in euro-zone economic activity and undermined by stock market gains in Japan. \par \par \uc2  An increase in Italy's purchasing managers' index in August, the second consecutive monthly rise, lifted the euro as high as $1.0625, its strongest since August 23. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has benefited from the PMI report as the data suggest that the weakest economy of core Europe is starting to recovery," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic advisor at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also bolstered after Bundesbank directorate member Edgar Meister said he saw stronger German growth in the second half of 1999 and an even stronger expansion in 2000. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar held within a quarter yen from Tuesday's seven-month lows near 109 yen as the yen was bolstered by a 2.10 percent rally in Japan's Nikkei stock average and in the absence of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  By 0733 GMT the euro was at $1.0635/40 from $1.0557/62 late in Europe on Tuesday, indifferent to a softening of the French August PMI but boosted further by a sharp rise in the German PMI. Both reports were released after the Italian one. \par \par \uc2  "We were desperate for some good news out of Italy, so that survey gave the initial boost to the euro," said Audrey-Childe Freeman, European economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "The French PMI was slightly disappointing, but the index is still above 50, which indicates expansion. Given the batch of positive data released yesterday, this PMI will not deteriorate the image of a healthy economic environment in France." \par \par \uc2  The Italian August PMI rose to 51.7 from 51.3 in July, while the French one softened to 54.55 from 55.93 a month ago. \par \par \uc2  The German August PMI, rose for the second consecutive month and showed the fasted input price rise in 18 months. \par \par \uc2  The optimistic European surveys lifted the euro against the yen as well. Euro/yen was last at 116.17/23 from 115.75/50 late on Tuesday in Europe and more than one percent above lifetime lows below 114 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar was at 109.25/34 yen compared with 109.55/65 in late European trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that, apart from the surge in Japanese stocks, the yen was benefiting from a potential upward revision of economic forecasts for Japan by the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  Hubert Neiss, Asia-Pacific director for the IMF, said on Wednesday the official 1999 IMF 0.25 percent growth forecast could be increased to 0.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  However, he added that the main threat to Japan's recovery was a further yen appreciation. His comments were echoed by remarks by top \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Zembei Mizoguchi. \par \par \uc2  But Yoshio Suzuki, a senior member of the Liberal Party, the junior coalition partner in the government, said the dollar's fall below 110 yen did not necessarily mean that the BOJ would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "So long as we are getting conflicting signals from the Japanese authorities, the general feeling is that the yen is going to appreciate further against the dollar," said Hawkins at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Europe the Swedish crown was supported against the euro and the yen by a strong rise in the country's August PMI. \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reutesr.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9101ghx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
