\par\par \b \uc2  Yen extends gains against the dollar, BOJ absent. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1999\par 23:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 1 (Reuters) - The yen charged to seven-month highs against the dollar on Wednesday, putting the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within reach of peaks not seen in three years. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan (BOJ) was noticeably absent from the market, tempting traders to see how far they can push Japanese authorities anxious to keep the yen from rising too quickly. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the BOJ doesn't show its hand, these guys are becoming increasingly emboldened to jam the dollar down," said Michael King, assistant Treasurer at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  After languishing in narrow trading ranges in subdued Tokyo and London trade, the dollar sliced past the psychologically significant 109 yen level to a low of 108.68. \par \par \uc2  Traders cited dollar selling by large investment funds in thin trading conditions, which set off technical triggers to push the dollar even lower. \par \par \uc2  By the end of the U.S. session the greenback had pared its losses to end at 109.15/20 yen, compared to 109.65/75 on Tuesday, but more declines were likely in the very near term, traders and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The early January low at 108.15 will likely be tested within the next week or so," said Martin Autotte, technical analyst at CIBC Wood Gundy in Montreal. \par \par \uc2  "A move above 110.50 would be a cause of concern to the bearish scenario. Otherwise we feel the bears are in control." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in June and July, although it has not been seen in more than a month after its efforts to stem yen gains proved ineffective. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had briefly perked up in Tokyo when Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said authorities would act against rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves and disturbing market factors. \par \par \uc2  But mere words had little lasting effect on the yen-hungry market. \par \par \uc2  A surge in Japanese stocks and positive outlook for Japan's economy has prompted investors to swap dollars and euros for yen to buy Japanese assets. That has propelled the yen up by 11.5 percent against the dollar since early July. \par \par \uc2  The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also slid sharply against the yen in tandem with the dollar, although it stayed above lifetime lows below 115 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally sidelined after an early burst of energy fizzled. \par \par \uc2  The euro had briefly rallied to a one-week high against the dollar of $1.0638 on supportive European economic data, especially German and Italian purchasing managers' indices. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank board member Edgar Meister also helped boost the euro when he said he saw stronger growth for German in the second half of 1999 and even greater expansion in 2000. \par \par \uc2  But a euro-zone wide manufacturing PMI, which rose marginally to 53.1 in August from 53.0 in July, disappointed euro bulls. \par \par \uc2  A lack of follow-through in the U.S. session further capped the euro's gains, and it wound down trade in New York at $1.0-575/80, barely up from $1.0561/66 in late Tuesday trade. \par \par \uc2  The British pound was little changed against the dollar at $1.6038/48, against $1.6045/55 previously, while against the Swiss franc the dollar stood at 1.5130/40 francs, down a touch from 1.5138/48. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv91019w8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
