\par\par \b \uc2  G7 Deputy Koch-Weser-3: \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Rates Discussed As Yen Gains \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1999\par 13:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's talks took place as the yen strengthened further against the dollar, sparking market speculation that central bankers could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem its rise. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already stepped into the market several times this year to cap the yen's persistent gains. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to around Y109 from Y111 early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the yen was a topic, Koch-Weser said, "You could imagine that exchange rates were discussed, as a part of the general surveillance discussion of the economic state of different countries." \par \par \uc2  He stressed that the two-day meeting was "routine" and preparatory. Koch-Weser declined to comment on most reporters questions about details of the meeting, deferring to the finance ministers, who will meet later in the month. \par \par \uc2  He said that Monday evening's meeting dealt with the state of the economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Those talks included representatives from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the International Monetary Fund and Finland, which currently represents the euro zone in its six-month presidency of the European Union. \par \par \uc2  The meeting Tuesday included only the G7 finance deputies. Topics included progress on improving international financial architecture and debt relief for poor countries. \par \par \uc2  Later Tuesday, G7 representatives will discuss Russia, Turkey, Latin America and Kosovo. -By G. Thomas Sims; 40-171577-115