\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW: LDP Aizawa -2:LDP Ohara: \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Unlikely \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hidenobu Kageyama \par \uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1999\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Two senior lawmakers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling Liberal Democratic Party have said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the recent strengthening of the yen at this time. \par \par \uc2  LDP lawmaker and former vice finance minister for administrative affairs Hideyuki Aizawa told Dow Jones Newswires in an interview Tuesday that it is now difficult for the finance ministry to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen because such action is not very effective. \par \par \uc2  "I think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not very effective," the lawmaker said. \par \par \uc2  "While (Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs) Haruhiko Kuroda seeks a stable yen, it is difficult to find out what is the best dollar/yen rate for Japanese firms," the LDP official added. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile Ichizo Ohara, a senior official at the LDP, said in an interview Monday that while he believes a further rise in the yen could hurt Japan's economy, the ministry won't likely take action in the immediate future unless the dollar weakens against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It is now difficult (for the MOF) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to weaken the yen) because the dollar/yen's drop is due to yen's strengthening, not due to dollar's weakening," Ohara said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 31-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par 