\par\par \b \uc2  OPTIONS -  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  vols pop higher on dollar tumble. \b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1999\par 20:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Aug 31 (Reuters) - Implied volatilities in the major dollar pairs popped higher Tuesday as the greenback slipped back toward seven-month lows versus the Japanese yen and one-week lows against the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid weakness in the U.S. stock market. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen fell back toward the overnight lows of 109 yen, while the euro climbed above the $1.06 level as the Dow Jones industrial average lost more than 100 points after the early release of stronger-than-forecast U.S. manufacturing data. \par \par \uc2  The National Association of Purchasing Management's manufacturing index rose to 54.2 in August from 53.4 in July. The prices index jumped to 59.8 from 54.7. \par \par \uc2  Stocks eventually found support and have since trimmed some losses after the initial spike lower, limiting the dollar's decline. \par \par \uc2  But volatility levels spiked, leaving one-month dollar/yen at 14.5/14.7 percent, up from 13.2/13.5 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  One-year dollar/yen volatility rose to 12.8/13.1 percent from 12.5/12.75 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Risk reversals are slanted for the yen calls at 2.7/2.9 from 2.25/2.6 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The biggest event so far is the 110 (yen) level was finally breached," said Masao Okada, chief options dealer at Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank. "That level was a big trigger level, and now that it has been breached today, the market condition has been dramatically changed." \par \par \uc2  Typically when a trigger level is very close to the current spot level, the options market becomes long gamma, Okada explained. \par \par \uc2  "A large exotic option with a 110 trigger level was coming off later this week," he said. "The market was extremely long gamma until (Monday and Tuesday). Dollar/yen has gotten out of the very, very thick web. Now it's much easier for dollar/yen to make a big move to either side." \par \par \uc2  If the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon, dollar/yen could post a "big jump," Okada added. \par \par \uc2  "If the BOJ allows dollar/yen to move lower doing nothing, I think 108 seems to be an immediate target," he continued. "And 108 is the next big trigger in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options market. It all depends on whether or not the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  or Bank of Japan does anything following the Tokyo market today. If they don't do anything, that will only accelerate dollar decline." \par \par \uc2  One-month euro/dollar volatility was at 10.2/10.3 percent, up from 9.55/9.8 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  One-year euro/dollar vols were at 9.75/9.95 percent, up from 9.5/9.7 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Risk reversals favour the euro calls at 0.5/0.6 from 0.05/0.25 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  ((Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750 \par \par \uc2  chicago.derivatives.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8v01f5k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
