\par\par \b \uc2  Yen set to steam ahead in absence of G7 action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1999\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The yen is likely to trample over other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless officials from the Group of Seven industrial nations surprise the markets with measures to combat bullishness about the Japanese unit, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  German Deputy Finance Minister Caio Koch-Weser said on Tuesday he and his counterparts from Britain, Canada, France, Italy, Japan and the United States had discussed the yen on the second day of their two-day meeting in Berlin. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said the foreign exchanges had so far seen nothing to curb the strength of the yen, which hit seven month peaks against the dollar and all-time highs against the euro even as the G7 deputies met. \par \par \uc2  Nor did they expect the meeting to produce anything to stop the yen's advance and the damage that could inflict on Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  "The market is not exactly quaking with fear at the moment despite the G7 deputies' meeting," said Paul Lambert, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  "Not all of the G7 authorities believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  works, particularly given that past history suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not succeed when monetary policy is not going in the same direction." \par \par \uc2  Lambert said the dollar therefore risked extending its slide to 105 yen in the next two weeks, about four yen below Tuesday's troughs. The yen has already risen over 14 percent against the dollar and 16 percent against the euro in the past three months. \par \par \uc2  No formal statement is expected from the G7 deputies meeting, which is preparing the ground for a G7 finance ministers' meeting in September on the sidelines of an International Monetary Fund/World Bank gathering. \par \par \uc2  At that time, the G7 will have to go beyond its well-worn formula - calling for exchange rates to remain in line with fundamentals - if it is to turn the tide against the yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "What people want to see is action," said Martin Squires, head of research at Rudolf Wolff & Co in London. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several occasions and this has done nothing to stem yen strength, so it is really going to need some sort of concerted policy shift." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least seven times since June 10, including once via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and once through the Federal Reserve. Still, the yen has strengthened nine percent against the dollar since it began its efforts. \par \par \uc2  The failure of solo Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the yen's advance makes it even more imperative that the G7 presents a coordinated front against yen bulls, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  This view was reinforced after a senior member of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party said he believed his country's representative at the G7 deputies meeting would be seeking support for joint U.S.-Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, the comments gave the dollar only fleeting support against the yen, with dealers quick to dismiss talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be launched around 105 yen. \par \par \uc2  While they remained wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said they would continue to target lower levels until they saw coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If they flagged 105 as an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, what they would effectively be saying is, 'Go short now lads and when it's four big figures lower we will help you buy it back,'" said a dealer at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "Unfortunately life is just not that simple. But it does look like the market is gunning for the year's lows around 108.20." ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8v01et8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
