\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar soars, then retreats versus yen in choppy US. \b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1999\par 20:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The dollar swung higher against the yen in midday U.S. trade on Thursday amid fresh market talk about the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to tame the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But a downmove in the U.S. stock market helped to take the shine off the dollar, with the Dow Jones industrial average sinking some 86 points. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to just under 112 yen, more than a full yen above overnight lows, before momentum stalled and the dollar retreated to 111.32/42 at 1400 EDT/1800 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "It's a completely rumour-loaded market today," said a New-York based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  Market talk focused on the upcoming Group of Seven meeting in late September, amid growing speculation about the prospect for joint U.S.-Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Some traders suggested an advance meeting of G7 deputies could be as soon as this weekend, although there was no confirmation from Washington. \par \par \uc2  "As the weekend approaches and trade thins out, no one wants to be short dollars, even though the instinct is to buy yen," said Mitsuaki Kataoka, vice president at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  The yen has risen about 10 percent against the dollar since early July, boosted by strong gains in the Tokyo stock market as expectations of economic recovery build steam. \par \par \uc2  The yen's appeal, traders say, reflects the strong performance of Japanese stocks and hedging of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk by Japanese institutional investors. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame yen strength at least seven times since June 10, fearing a rapid yen rise will hurt the nascent economic recovery, but it has not been seen in the market since July 21. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the euro stayed above the overnight lows near $1.04, hovering at $1.0450/57. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the market had shrugged off data showing U.S. economic growth had slowed to its lowest level in a year in the second quarter, in line with economists' forecasts. \par \par \uc2  Gross domestic product expanded at a revised 1.8 percent annual rate, less than half the first quarter's 4.3 percent advance. \par \par \uc2  "The GDP didn't have any effect whatsoever - it was as expected," said Dennis Heidt, chief dealer at Banque Paribas. "This week we've already had news with much greater impact, such as the Fed rate move and gyrations in the stock market." \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve's quarter-point rate hike of two key short-term interest rates on Tuesday gave the dollar a boost against the euro, Swiss franc and British pound. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier left its key refinancing rate unchanged at 2.50 percent, as expected. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market's moves were also exaggerated by thin trading conditions. \par \par \uc2  In other trade, the dollar drifted against the British pound to $1.5872/82 as U.S. trade got underway compared to $1.5845/55 in late New York trade Wednesday. The greenback slipped to 1.5318/28 Swiss francs from 1.5373/83 francs. \par \par \uc2  ((-Lida Poletz, North American Treasury Desk +1 212 859 1868)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8q01sxz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
