\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar gets mixed results a day after FOMC. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1999\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The dollar kept its lead against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early New York trade on Wednesday after markets put a positive spin overnight on the hike in U.S. short term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still struggling against the upward momentum of the Japanese yen, and dealers looked for more dollar declines toward the psychological 110 yen level. \par \par \uc2  Analysts linked the dollar's gains versus the euro, Swiss franc and sterling to the Federal Reserve's Tuesday decision to raise the federal funds and discount rates by a quarter point while keeping a neutral bias on future monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  "The way the market is reading this short term is that the Fed is done raising rates. That's good for stocks and bonds, which in turn is good for the dollar against the euro," said Paul Podolsky, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BankBoston. \par \par \uc2  A widening interest rate differential between the United States and Europe would also be dollar-supportive, he said. \par \par \uc2  Benign inflation data from euro-zone heavyweights Germany and Italy this week supported the view the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will leave rates alone for the rest of the year. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 EDT/1230 GMT, the euro stood at $1.0409/14, approaching five-week lows against the dollar and down sharply from $1.0532/39 in late Tuesday trade. \par \par \uc2  A drift lower on Wall Street later took some of the shine off the dollar after U.S. trade got underway, but it still remained well above levels seen late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "It's starting to look like the euro's rise to $1.08 earlier this month was a correction, and that maybe we all got too optimistic about Europe," said a trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The British pound crumpled to $1.5845/55 from $1.5932/42, having slipped to four-week lows during European trade. And the dollar soared close to five-week highs against the Swiss franc, to stand at 1.5372/82, against 1.5185/95 previously. \par \par \uc2  There was no pessimism surrounding the yen, however, which has won favour from investors thanks to the buoyant Japanese stock market amid expectations of economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 111.03/13 yen as U.S. trade got underway, compared to 111.23/28 in late Tuesday dealings. \par \par \uc2  The market was irresistibly drawn to the 110 yen level, traders said, where many would expect Japanese monetary authorities to think about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had suffered a violent dip to seven-month lows around 110.40 yen in Tokyo trade, followed quickly by a two-yen leap. Traders dismissed rumours that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar retreated from its highs. \par \par \uc2  Sharp zigzag movements in the euro against the dollar and yen in early U.S. trade reflected low market liquidity, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In other trade the Australian dollar edged down to $0.6315/20, from $0.6365/70, while the U.S. dollar rose to Canadian $1.4935/45 from $1.4894/04. \par \par \uc2  ((-North American Treasury Desk +1 212 859 1868)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8p01zia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
