\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar gains broadly, except vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1999\par 13:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The dollar gained broadly on Wednesday as the market began to appreciate the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate edge after Tuesday's Federal Reserve rate hike, although the buoyant yen bucked the trend. \par \par \uc2  While muted reactions in U.S. asset markets to the Fed's decision - to raise key interest rates by 25 basis points while maintaining a neutral policy bias - initially disappointed dollar bulls overnight, the higher U.S. rates made the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  look generally more attractive, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was soft, however, due to growing optimism over an economic recovery in Japan and lingering concerns over the U.S. trade deficit. An absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also made the dollar vulnerable against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's pretty much 'buy dollars against everything' - everything except the yen, which is a special case right now," said Minoru Ozawa, head of trading at Sakura Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar shed one cent from overnight highs and traded at $1.0443/48 at 1017 GMT, within striking distance of Tuesday's $1.0390 five-week low. Sterling was probing four week lows in the mid-$1.58 area, last trading at $1.5860/70. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' weakness accelerated the persistent euro/yen selling by Japanese investors trying to hedge their European asset holdings, sending euro/yen to life lows for the second straight day. \par \par \uc2  The euro was last trading at 116.02/17 yen against 117.19/29 late in Europe on Tuesday. The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly fell below 116 for the first time since it was launched in January, touching a low of 115.78 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was flirting with the 111-yen area, unable to escape the gravity of a seven-month trough hit overnight at 110.41 yen. It was last trading at 111.05/10 yen against 111.53/56 late in Europe on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Despite seemingly unstoppable bullishness on the yen, the market remained nervous over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Indeed, rumour of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying caused the greenback to spike up above 112 yen from the lows in Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  "I don't know if they (Japanese authorities) have accepted that this is a half-year thing...or if at some point it will become intolerable for them," said a trader at a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  He said Japanese investors' position-cleaning ahead of their half-year book-closing at the end of September was the market's main driving force at the moment and that the flows could reverse after September. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Ministry officials declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumour. \par \par \uc2  Ozawa at Sakura Bank said the euro looked extremely vulnerable and could retest the early July life lows near $1.01 and eventually the $1.00 level against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders added that the 113.80 yen area in euro/yen was the equivalent of the 58.20 yen low in mark/yen from April 1995. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8p01y49\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
