\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar struggles vs yen after rumour-driven rally. \b0\par\par\uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1999\par 06:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The dollar was struggling against the yen by Tokyo midday on Wednesday, pressured by follow-through sales after an early rally on rumours of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost steam, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at around 111 yen, with many interbank operators still waiting for chances to buy the yen, given brighter prospects for Japan's economy, they said. \par \par \uc2  A wave of bids, mainly led by Japanese pension funds, boosted the dollar to a high of 112.40 yen in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Initially, operators thought the dollar's rise was the result of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which intensified the uptrend, but the rumour quickly faded. \par \par \uc2  At 0323 GMT, the dollar stood at 110.93/96 yen compared with 111.23/28 yen in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's rapid rise came right around the time when (Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko) Kuroda's comments were splashing across the screens. That intensified speculation of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But after the market found out that Japanese pension funds had bought in relatively large amounts through trust banks, active sales by U.S. operators and Japanese life insurers quickly hammered the dollar from its high," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market's thinness may have exaggerated the uptrend after pension funds' bids. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Bureau, declined to comment about the rumour. \par \par \uc2  He also declined to comment on policy-making by the U.S. authorities and repeatedly said he could not comment on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I can only say we are watching movements in the market carefully and will take appropriate action as needed," he said. \par \par \uc2  In early trade, the dollar slumped to a fresh seven-month low of 110.40 yen, after the greenback's rally overnight was limited below 113 yen following the Federal Reserve's credit-tightening. \par \par \uc2  The Fed hiked its fed funds rate target level by 25 basis points to 5.25 percent and kept a neutral bias. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also raised its discount rate by the same amount to 4.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  U.S. asset markets gave a muted reaction to the Fed's long expected rate hike. \par \par \uc2  Activity thinned by late morning as many operators refrained from taking fresh positions after the volatile trade in dollar/yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was expected to carry that mood in afternoon trade, with dealers expecting the dollar to fluctuate tightly near 111 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's bullish trend stays intact, but the market will be a bit cautious about testing the dollar below 110.50 yen. The dollar's surge today shows the market's intense caution towards the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a Japanese trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's falls below 110.50 yen should take it to a key psychological support of 110.00 yen, where massive option-related sales are rumoured placed. \par \par \uc2  "The point is whether we are going to see the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at below 110 yen. Trading in dollar/yen should get very nervous when the dollar approaches that level," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  The market showed a muted reaction to the Ministry of International Trade and Industry's index of overall business activity for June released earlier on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The market considers the data a clue in forecasting the April-June GDP figures due around September 10, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The index showed a fall of 0.4 percent in the April-June quarter - largely due to a downward revision for April to May - which was in line with estimates for GDP but was a disappointment to some analysts who had looked for a slightly firmer outcome. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Trade Ministry data showed Japan's July trade surplus fell 4.6 percent year-on-year but was still above forecasts at 1.249 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  The market reacted little to the results, they said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trapped in tight ranges throughout the day. At 0401 GMT, the euro stood at $1.0516/21 against $1.0532/39 in late New York on Tuesday. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8p01xdp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
