\par\par \b \uc2  Yen-Weakening  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Requires Unlikely Teamwork \b0\par\par\uc2  By Marianne Sullivan \par \uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1999\par 19:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Not even the Bank of Japan will blunt the dollar's slide against the yen this time around. \par \par \uc2  As the dollar slides toward Y110.00, what many consider Japan's mystical line in the sand, markets can't seem to let go of the fear that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  - as it had throughout June and July - to prevent what it called the premature appreciation of the yen. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -shy markets got a bit of a jolt this week when Forbes printed a column suggesting all signs seemed to be pointing to a coordinated U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - "the Plaza Accord in Reverse." David Roche, chief strategist at London-based Independent Strategy, presented unsterlized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a way to match the need of both \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. to reverse the trend of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Warburg Dillon Read's head of global stategy, Larry Hatheway, was quick to rebut the likelihood of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , emphasizing four separate institutions which "don't see eye to eye" on the issue would have to be involved. The U.S. Federal Reserve Bank, the U.S. Treasury, Bank of Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would comprise the unlikely team. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players mind especially before the Fed's Open Market Committee decides on interest rates. A relief rally in U.S. markets, which could result from a Fed decision to raise rates by 25 basis points while keeping its bias at neutral, could present ideal conditions for an effective yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Such an effort would cash in on the momentum already in place. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The worry that Japanese authorities might be planning to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par support of the dollar around the same time that the FOMC makes its\par announcement was dispelled by Haruhiko Kuroda, vice finance minister for\par international affairs, earlier Tuesday. He repeated there is no\par relationship between the FOMC's schedule and Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par policy.\par -By Marianne Sullivan; 201-938-4385\par email: marianne.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-08-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1728GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8o069is\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
