\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Euro shines, wary yen in retreat. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1999\par 12:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The euro firmed to one-week highs above $1.0650 on Friday and rose two percent from the previous day's life lows against the yen as yen bulls stayed away amid renewed wariness of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Thursday's strong German Ifo survey pointing to a brighter economic outlook for Europe and the larger-than-expected U.S. trade deficit were the main factors behind the euro's two-cent leap in as many days. \par \par \uc2  "The strength of the Ifo survey was one supportive factor for euro/dollar, but not the only factor," said Patrick O'Sullivan, economist at AIB Group in Dublin. \par \par \uc2  "The widening of the U.S. trade gap is a concern for the U.S. and is not helping the dollar." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro was helped by supportive remarks by Bundesbank president designate Ernst Welteke. \par \par \uc2  Welteke told a German magazine that the end of weak European growth was in sight and that the euro rebound could be strong, as dollar strength was incompatible with the high U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currenct\b0 \highlight\uc2  account deficit. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar recovered one yen from a seven-month low of 110.65 hit on Thursday as traders become more wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action as the yen approached psychological resistance at 110 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "People believe there is a threshold for dollar/yen beyond which the Japanese authories would be unhappy," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers in London. "The question is: where is this threshold?" \par \par \uc2  By 1034 GMT, the dollar was at 111.60/65 yen against 111.11/13 late in Europe on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0670/78, its highest since August 13, from $1.0639/46 late in Europe on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, euro/yen was at 119.12/27 compared with 118.24/28 in late European trading on Thursday and against a life low of 116.52 hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  News BOJ Deputy Governor Yutaka Yamaguchi will visit the United States for ten days from Saturday had sparked fears overnight of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy coordination between Japan and the U.S., helping the dollar to rebound against the yen. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said that until now there had been no indication by the U.S. authorities that they would be ready to take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if dollar/yen weakened so much as to undermine Japan's recovery," said Tony Norfield, head of global treasury research at ABN AMRO in London \par \par \uc2  "However at the moment they (the U.S.) are more concerned with what is going on domestically." \par \par \uc2  Ichizo Ohara, a senior member of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party, said on Friday that a dollar drop below 110 yen would be problematic, reinforcing the view that 110 was the level which could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if breached. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was detected selling yen for dollars or euros at least seven times between June and July, but despite this round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it had not managed to brake the yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8k0278g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
