\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Real Flows Driving Yen Strength Vs Euro \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 08:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y117.14, down from Y117.81 in New York late Wednesday and below Y118.20 in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro later fell below Y117, as stop-loss orders were triggered pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a fresh low of Y116.85. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue to suffer against the yen at the expense of reallocation of investment funds into Japanese assets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There are real money flows moving into Japan from Europe. It appears that until that subsides, the yen is going to keep getting stronger," Suzuki said. \par \par \uc2  Market sentiment is also geared toward further yen strength against the dollar. The U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to fall to Y110 next week on continued hedge selling by Japanese investors and foreign demand for yen, said Hikari Sekioka, a vice president at Sakura Bank. \par \par \uc2  "There aren't many factors that can change this trend," he said, adding that a break of Y110 would set mid-Y108 as next target. \par \par \uc2  While many players are keeping an eye out for action by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most said that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own won't be able to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  The chance of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  involving the U.S. Federal Reserve still remains a slim possibility, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Kazuteru Hasegawa, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of America in Tokyo, said the U.S. won't likely agree to joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  until it sees proof in the form of an extra budget that Japan is continuing to boost domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. will (ascertain) Japan's effort and then move in the market," Hasegawa said. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6015, down from $1.6027 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6043 in London late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott; 813-5255-2929; amscott@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0603GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8j064iq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
