\par\par \b \uc2  OUTLOOK-Reuters Asia Business at 0600 GMT. \b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2     Following are some of the main business news stories (all \par \par \uc2  times GMT) \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      MARKETS \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE - Most Asian share markets inch higher despite \par \par \uc2  U.S. drop on Wednesday but Tokyo loses more than one percent on \par \par \uc2  the yen's appreciation against the dollar and the euro, with \par \par \uc2  export-oriented high-technology and electronics shares coming \par \par \uc2  under pressure; the dollar drops below the 112 yen level to its \par \par \uc2  lowest since January. \par \par \uc2      ** Spot cover of major individual market moves \par \par \uc2      ** Wraps on regional share and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  action \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - Yen continues its surge against dollar and euro, \par \par \uc2  raising fears that Japanese monetary authorities will step in \par \par \uc2  to stop its rise to prevent the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from hurting \par \par \uc2  the nation's exporters. \par \par \uc2      ** Focus story on likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2      LONDON/FRANKFURT/PARIS - Wall Street weakness, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  turmoil and hesitation ahead of next weeks's Federal Reserve \par \par \uc2  policy meetings should make for caution in European markets. \par \par \uc2      ** Spot coverage, wraps through trading day \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      JAPAN BANKING GIANTS CONSIDER ALLIANCE \par \par \uc2      TOKYO - Japanese banking giants Fuji Bank, Dai-ichi Kangyo \par \par \uc2  Bank and Industrial Bank of Japan say they are considering a \par \par \uc2  comprehensive alliance that may include setting up a joint \par \par \uc2  holding company. A three-way partnership would create the \par \par \uc2  world's largest financial group in terms of deposits and \par \par \uc2  debentures. \par \par \uc2      ** Spot coverage, full story \par \par \uc2      ** Analysis \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      SOUTH KOREA Q2 GDP UP 9.8 PCT ON YEAR \par \par \uc2      SEOUL - South Korea's gross domestic product grew 9.8 \par \par \uc2  percent between second quarters of 1998 and 1999, against 7.2 \par \par \uc2  percent decline previous year, surpassing expectations. \par \par \uc2      ** Table of Q2 GDP figures \par \par \uc2      ** Spot on analysts' reactions \par \par \uc2      ** Wrap of GDP figures with analyst comments, outlook - - - \par \par \uc2      FOREIGN BANKS MADE NO PROMISES TO KOREA'S DAEWOO \par \par \uc2      SEOUL - Foreign banks have not promised to refrain from \par \par \uc2  taking legal action against South Korea's troubled Daewoo \par \par \uc2  Group, foreign banker says. \par \par \uc2      ** Fresh look at foreign bankers' views on debt-laden \par \par \uc2  Daewoo Group's restructuring \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      BANK BALI LOAN FEE RETURNED BUT CONTROVERSY LINGERS \par \par \uc2      JAKARTA - A controversial loan fee is returned in full to \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's Bank Bali but questions over the matter heat up, \par \par \uc2  creating a scandal that has even threatened President B.J. \par \par \uc2  Habibie's chances at relection. \par \par \uc2      ** New story \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      NEWSCORP BULLISH ON U.S. TELEVISION MARKET PROSPECTS \par \par \uc2      SYDNEY - Global media group News Corp Ltd is bullish on its \par \par \uc2  prospects in the U.S. television market, with all divisions \par \par \uc2  expected to improve this year except film, analysts say \par \par \uc2      - Analysis on outlook for News Corp after it announced \par \par \uc2  lower annual profits. \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      CHINA SHOWS SHARP DOWNTURN IN FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT \par \par \uc2      BEIJING - China records sharp downturn in actual and \par \par \uc2  contracted foreign direct investment in first seven months, but \par \par \uc2  remains mum on when it will restart key talks on joining the \par \par \uc2  World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2      ** Story based on foreign trade ministry news conference \par \par \uc2  with analysts comments \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      QANTAS ANNOUNCES SHARP JUMP IN YEAR PROFIT \par \par \uc2      SYDNEY - Australia's flagship carrier Qantas Airways Ltd \par \par \uc2  announces 38 percent jump in year profit in a competitive \par \par \uc2  aviation market and says its stronger revenue trend was \par \par \uc2  continuing in the new financial year. ** Wrap on results \par \par \uc2  including interview with chief executive James Strong. \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE EXPORTS, MANUFACTURING SEEN RISING \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE - Singapore should see robust manufacturing \par \par \uc2  growth this year and future growth will come primarily from \par \par \uc2  chemical and precision engineering sectors, Economic \par \par \uc2  Development Board chairman says, while a Reuters poll shows the \par \par \uc2  city-state's non-oil exports in July are likely to see robust \par \par \uc2  growth of 12 percent year-on-year fuelled by strong economic \par \par \uc2  growth and a turnaround in global electronics. \par \par \uc2      ** Interview with EDB Chairman Philip Yeo on growth \par \par \uc2  prospects \par \par \uc2      ** Story on poll, reasons for expected jump in export \par \par \uc2  numbers and where contributions to growth are coming from \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      THAILAND ADVANCES ON CORPORATE DEBT RESTRUCTURING \par \par \uc2      BANGKOK - Thailand's corporate debt restructuring has made \par \par \uc2  steady progress after three months of enforcement of new \par \par \uc2  bankruptcy and foreclosure laws, Justice Ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials say. \par \par \uc2      ** Story on outlook for debt restructuring at troubled Thai \par \par \uc2  companies \par \par \uc2      - - - - \par \par \uc2      If you have any queries, please call: \par \par \uc2      Singapore (65) 870-3815 \par \par \uc2      Comments to: asia.newseds@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8j024as\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
