\par\par \b \uc2  US  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  possible if US assets hurt-Merrill. \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1999\par 08:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - A U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the beleaguered dollar is possible when U.S. authorities become concerned about stability of its own asset markets, Merrill Lynch's senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Neil MacKinnon said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  MacKinnon said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a lone attempt to try to push the dollar higher against the yen, was not successful despite the bank's heavy spending of as much as $30 billion. \par \par \uc2  "Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by U.S. and Japanese authorities, I think, would be effective," he told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "But for that to happen, American authorities would have to see clear evidence of continued deterioration in global asset prices. In particular, they have to see evidence that their own stock and bond markets have been severely destabilised by a sharp appreciation of the yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  London-based MacKinnon is in Tokyo as part of an Asia-wide trip. \par \par \uc2  Given the dollar's fall below the key chart support of 113.70 yen, verbal warning is likely to increase, and the dollar is highly likely to be protected from falling lower than 110 yen, or possibly 108 yen, MacKinnon said. \par \par \uc2  But without joint dollar buying by U.S. and Japanese authorities, the dollar could plunge to 105 yen, he said. \par \par \uc2  As for the euro, which has been renewing record lows against the yen this week, there is a downside room to around 117 yen, MacKinnon said. \par \par \uc2  There is a possibility for the yen to make further gains against the euro after the European unit's recent fall to $1.05 level from $1.07/1.08 level. But the euro has a solid support at $1.0350, giving scope for some outperformance of the yen against the euro to around 117, he said. \par \par \uc2  Mackinnon said, however, he expected the euro to recover in the near future when European economic data shows improvement. Anticipation of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) rate hike may also heighten after ECB members are back from summer holidays, he said. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.news room@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8i02elk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
