\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr,euro down vs yen, Japanese step up hedge sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1999\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The dollar and euro were down against the yen in late Tokyo on Wednesday, as nervous Japanese exporters and investors stepped up hedge selling. \par \par \uc2  The yen was also buoyed by expectations of more foreign investor purchases of Japanese stocks, but vague talk of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  trimmed its gains. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 113.80/85 yen at 0623 GMT, down from 113.93/03 yen in New York late on Tuesday. It briefly slipped as low as 113.63 yen, its lowest level since August 5. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 119.59/76 yen, versus 119.84 yen in late New York. It briefly fell to a fresh lifetime low of 119.40 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Actually, sentiment towards the dollar is not so bad, after the U.S. Treasury market rallied overnight on (U.S.) consumer price data," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  "But the good U.S. data was overwhelmed by growing yen-buying pressures," he said. \par \par \uc2  The price of the benchmark 30-year U.S. Treasury bond rose more than a full point on Tuesday after the release of data showing a 0.3 percent rise in the July U.S. Consumer Price Index. \par \par \uc2  The CPI data buoyed U.S. asset markets by backing the market's view that the U.S. Federal Reserve's next interest rate hike is likely to be its last for this year. \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters stepped up dollar sales for yen as they were increasingly wary about fulfilling their hedging needs for the second half of the fiscal year to next March 31. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of Japanese exporters are eager to hedge their export proceeds for the October-March period at a dollar rate of no lower than 110 yen," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But it would be difficult do so using \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards if the spot dollar rate fell any further," he added. \par \par \uc2  The euro was battered against the yen by selling by Japanese investors, such as investment trust funds and life insurers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also weighed down by expectations of continued buying of Japanese stocks by European investors. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei average closed up 32.17 points or 0.18 percent at 17,892.26 on Wednesday, after earlier breaching the 18,000-point barrier for the first time in nearly one month. But the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was relatively stable against the dollar. The euro was at $1.0504/08 against $1.0511/18 in New York late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers cited vague talk of euro bids from European central banks around $1.0490. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro was likely to remain well-supported against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the release of a July business climate survey by Germany's Ifo economic research institute on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Thirteen economists polled by Reuters on Monday expected, on average, an improvement to 93.5 in July in the Ifo index. In the June survey, the headline figure for western Germany rose to 92.9 from 90.5 in May, hitting its highest level since September 1998 and helping to trigger a rally in the euro above $1.08. \par \par \uc2  The market was still wary about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Haruhiko Kuroda, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice finance minister for international affairs, said Japan would take decisive action if needed to avoid a premature rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  "A premature yen rise is unfavourable for the Japanese and world economies... If necessary, we will take timely and decisive action," Kuroda said. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar and the euro extended losses after very brief recovery on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk. \par \par \uc2  At 0709 GMT, the dollar was at 113.30/40 yen and the euro at 119.05/16 yen. \par \par \uc2  The market was unmoved by minutes of the BOJ's June 28 Policy Board meeting, released on Wednesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  They showed that the board rejected by a vote of 8-1 a proposal to ease credit further by setting targets of a one percent inflation rate and 10 percent annual growth in the monetary base. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8i02a9i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
