\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah surges as yen lifts Asia. \b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1999\par 13:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah climbed further against the dollar on Wednesday as the surging yen supported emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board. \par \par \uc2  The yen hit six-month highs against the dollar, bursting through 113 to the greenback with no sign of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper the rise. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ticked upwards against the dollar on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's coat-tails, staying roughly in line with the yen as a major regional trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the rupiah stood out, chiselling some four percent off the dollar and pushing past 7,300 at one point before settling back slightly. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said they saw little specific reason behind Wednesday's rise, although the International Monetary Fund's call for a thorough investigation into irregularities at PT Bank Bali may have helped sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Although the surge owed much to the rupiah's usual volatility and low liquidity, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked set for further strengthening in the medium term, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Official comments that 6,000-6,500 is a reasonable level are perfectly believable, so that's another 25 percent upside from here," said Graham Neilson, Asia economist at Banque Paribas in London. \par \par \uc2  "For the longer term I'm quite happy with a fair value around 6,500-6,700, assuming the yen and the rest of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are stable." \par \par \uc2  But some were more bearish on the rupiah, arguing that Indonesia's economy remained shaky and political risk was high ahead of presidential elections in November. \par \par \uc2  "It's a bit like Russian Eurobonds - if you're going to trade them you can make money, but don't seriously tell me you're investing," said Nick Douch, emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  Neilson at Paribas said emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were seeing increased volatility in general, because of bottoming regional interest rates and a wider reappraisal of risk premiums. \par \par \uc2  But a cyclical downturn in dollar/yen and an easing of overplayed worries about a Chinese devaluation should provide good medium-term support. \par \par \uc2  "All these Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should strengthen against the dollar in the next six to nine months," he said, adding that the rupiah could pass 6,000 to the dollar in that time and head towards 5,000 in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  Despite support from the yen, not all Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were sparkling. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht remained in a bearish mood, lingering around 10-month lows on worries over state-run Krung Thai Bank and wider banking sector woes. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said it had not been in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, but was watching the situation closely. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to halt a sharp baht slide. \par \par \uc2  Most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  outside Asia marked time in quiet, holiday-season trade. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty eased cautiously against its trading basket ahead of the monthly meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (RPP). \par \par \uc2  It was quoted around 3.18 percent above basket parity by mid-morning, compared with late Tuesday's 3.22 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said they did not expect the RPP to announce any change in interest rates or the pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's crawl, currently set to devalue at 0.3 percent per month, although it might call for toughening on the fiscal front. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown paused in what analysts saw as a continuing uptrend against the euro, based on solid investment inflows. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.21   36.16   0.15%    4.06%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.16    4.15   0.26%    2.32%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 253.02  252.74   0.11%    0.73%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 44.49   44.55  -0.13%    3.47%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 16,070  16,080  -0.06%   46.76%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab   4.42    4.36   1.26%   12.34%\par South Africa\tab \tab    6.12    6.11   0.04%  