\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS - Euro off new low of Y120.77 in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1999\par 06:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 17 (Reuters) - After sinking to a record low against the yen, the euro rebounded slightly by midday on Tuesday in Tokyo on buybacks by earlier sellers, including U.S. operators. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at 121.33/49 yen at 0330 GMT after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier broke through key chart support at 121 yen and dropped to an all-time low of 120.77 yen in early Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded around 121.21 yen in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The euro dropped amid thin trade. That's typical early in the morning," said a senior trader at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Foreign speculators sold euros in early trading to trigger stop-loss selling around 121 yen, and that was followed by light selling by Japanese investment trusts to hedge their holdings of European financial assets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Light euro selling for the yen by Japanese exporters was also detected. \par \par \uc2  But caution over possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) kept the euro from falling further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's rise to a record high against the euro has certainly sharpened the market's alertness against possible BOJ action," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June to buy euro against the yen via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said on Tuesday there was no change in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "I will not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels," Kuroda told reporters. "There is no change in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda also said that a rise in Japanese stock prices was not necessarily a reason for the yen to rise. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8h02j9k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
