\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr, euro off lows vs yen, market wary of U.S. CPI. \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1999\par 03:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The dollar and the euro were off their lows against the yen in early Tokyo trade on Tuesday, after earlier slipping on euro selling for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Although the yen's outlook remained bullish amid expectations of further hedge selling of the euro by Japanese exporters and yen demand from European investors, operators were cautious ahead of the release of the U.S. consumer price index (CPI) later on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 114.67/70 yen at 0034 GMT, off its earlier low of 114.35 yen. The euro was at 121.01/10 yen, after earlier falling to a fresh lifetime low of 120.77 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Some overseas speculators sold euro to trigger stop-loss orders around 121 yen. But the euro bounced back on short-covering after setting new lows," said a dealer for a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Light euro selling for the yen by Japanese exporters was also detected earlier, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Many Japanese exporter clients still have not been able to fulfil all of their hedging needs in the euro/yen. So their selling interest is likely to limit euro/yen gains," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  There was also demand for the yen from European investors looking to buy more Japanese stocks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In addition to U.S. CPI data, the market was wary about possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's rise to a record high against the euro has certainly sharpened the market's alertness against possible BOJ action," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June to buy euro against the yen via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said on Tuesday there was no change in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "I will not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels," Kuroda told reporters on the way to his office. "There is no change in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy." \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stock and bond markets failed to set direction for dollar/yen, as their price moves were relatively stable on Tuesday morning. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei average of 225 leading shares was down 0.09 percent at 17,810.76 at 0052 GMT, after gaining 1.84 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The key March 10-year Japanese government bond futures contract was down 0.26 at 127.45. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market will be watching for comments from a regular news conference by BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami at 0600 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said in its monthly report for August that Japan's economy has stopped declining, but there were no signs yet of a self-sustainable recovery in private demand. The report also said that a rise in the yen was beginning to dampen Japan's exports. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0555/58 at 0057 GMT, slightly down from $1.0570/75 in New York late on Monday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8h02j41\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
