\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr softer vs yen as euro/yen slips to fresh low. \b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1999\par 01:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The dollar was softer against the yen in early Asia on Tuesday, indirectly weighed down by the continued weakness of the euro against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 114.50/53 yen at 2301 GMT, down from 114.60/70 yen in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 121.08/22 yen, after slipping to a fresh lifetime low of 120.77 yen in earlier trade. \par \par \uc2  The single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was battered by expectations of further hedge sales by Japanese exporters and yen demand by European investors looking to invest in Japanese stocks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Some overseas speculators sold euro for yen, apparently to trigger rumoured stop-loss sales between 120.50 yen and 121 yen," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  But the euro pared losses on short-covering, as the market was wary about possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against both the dollar and the euro by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June to buy euro against the yen via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There may be more stop-loss sell orders, but people would be cautious about testing them as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might act," the city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said many Tokyo players may refrain from trading aggressively ahead of the release later on Tuesday of the U.S. consumer price index (CPI) for July. \par \par \uc2  "As the CPI could strongly move U.S. asset markets, people are reluctant to trade actively," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast, on average, a rise of 0.3 percent in CPI for July. Core CPI excluding volatile food and energy prices is forecast to have risen 0.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve is widely expected to raise its key short-term interest rate by a quarter percentage point next week regardless of the outcome of the CPI. \par \par \uc2  But soft CPI data would still be supportive for U.S. asset markets, and therefore for the dollar, as it could fuel expectations that the Fed might not need to raise interest rates further in the autumn, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market will also be watching Tokyo stocks and bonds for clues to dollar/yen during Asian trading hours, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, gains in Tokyo share prices and rises in Japanese government bond yields were cited as partly responsible for the dollar's fall of more than one yen in Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  The market will also be watching for comments from a regular news conference by BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami at 0600 GMT, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0564/67 at 2335 GMT, slightly softer compared with $1.0570/75 in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "As long as support at $1.05 holds, I think the euro/dollar rate will remain on an uptrend," said a trust bank dealer. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8g02j1b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
