\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen surges, then pares gains in nervous U.S. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1999\par 15:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The dollar bounced higher against the Japanese yen in early trading as jittery dealers initially speculated a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be behind the buying but then said the move was caused only by a large buy order. \par \par \uc2  The dollar surged from its 114.71/81 opening level to a session high of 116.20 but soon came off again to trade near 115.80/90. "There was some speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying but no one has seen anything, instead I think it was a large order from a U.S. corporate player," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had already been gaining ground against the yen and euro after softer than expected U.S. PPI data helped boost the recently battered bond market by calming some of the market's fears of an imminent U.S. interest rate hike. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers have been on the lookout for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said overnight that he continued to watch the markets carefully. \par \par \uc2  "I would have thought today might be a good day for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Refco Group Ltd analyst Mike Malpede said. \par \par \uc2  However dealers said the gains were very orderly, suggesting the Bank of Japan was probably not behind the move. \par \par \uc2  Norwest Bank chief trader John Beerling said, "It felt more orderly than (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). Even though it was a pretty big move, there seemed to be prices all the way up." \par \par \uc2  Technicians had predicted the dollar would test as high as 116.20, as part of its recent recovery. Overnight the dollar was supported near 114.50. \par \par \uc2  ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8d02off\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
