\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar recovers in U.S. amid softer PPI data. \b0\par\par\uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1999\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The dollar dipped at the start of U.S. trading but quickly switched gears, paring losses against the yen and turning up against the euro as softer than expected U.S. inflation data boosted recently battered asset markets. \par \par \uc2  Producer prices rose 0.2 percent while the volatile core rate, which excludes food and energy, was unchanged in July. In June the headline rate fell 0.1 percent while the core rate eased 0.2 percent. U.S. Treasuries also jumped on the news. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's healthy 0.7 percent jump in July retail sales had sparked fears of stronger PPI data which would have fuelled more talk of a near term interest rate hike. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar has gotten quite bid and I think it has keyed on the reversal in the bond market which I think will spill over into the equity market," said Ricardo Gomes, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Republic National Bank. \par \par \uc2  In fact the steady gains were so pronounced in dollar/yen trading that dealers briefly feared a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be behind the move as the dollar roared up over a full yen to its session high at 116.20. \par \par \uc2  Even as traders remained nervous about the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said this move appeared too orderly to have been prompted by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It felt more orderly than (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). Even though it was a pretty big move, there seemed to be prices all the way up," said Norwest Bank chief dealer John Beerling. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was bruised in overnight trading when Japan revised an already strong 1.9 percent January to March gross domestic product report to 2 percent. This helped push the pair to 114.71/81 at the start from Thursday's 115.50/60 close. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  became the buzzword again overnight as Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he was watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Often, dealers said, this sort of talk has been interpreted as hints that more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the way. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the Bank of Japan would need help to make any yen sales effective, but predicted the United States is not ready to assist. \par \par \uc2  "I think it is unlikely that the U.S. would help now especially after President Clinton said he was not alarmed by the dollar's recent decline," Citibank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Bob Sinche said. \par \par \uc2  Some technicians had called for short-term gains to 116.20 but were not surprised when this level offered resistance. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also zipped higher against the euro, coming close to the key $1.0550 level. \par \par \uc2  After euro/dollar surged to a recent high near $1.0820 from its life low near $1.0104, dealers had expected a correction within the correction to about $1.0550. The pair started trading at $1.0663/70, only modestly changed from Thursday's $1.0661/68 close. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar was similarly flat against the Swiss franc, opening at 1.5010/20 from 1.5005/15 on Thursday before jumping to 1.5160/70. The British pound inched up to $1.6110/20 from $1.6103/08 but then dipped to $1.6050/60. \par \par \uc2  The commodity based \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also inched higher against the dollar initially. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar rose to $0.6515/20 from $0.6493/98 while the dollar dipped against the Canadian dollar to C$1.4820/30 from C$1.4845/55. \par \par \uc2  ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8d02gdq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
