\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar firm as assets keep nerve. \b0\par\par\uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1999\par 18:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The dollar hit two-week highs against the yen, euro and Swiss franc in Europe on Thursday as investors in U.S. assets absorbed the idea of a near-term tightening by the U.S. Federal Reserve, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback has reversed a weakening trend which had been fuelled by expectations of a U.S. rate rise this month, a move which markets feared would prompt foreign investors to divest U.S. stocks and bonds. But a rate increase was no longer seen as necessarily negative for the dollar, analysts said. "The message is the economy is slowing down, it might need some help from the Fed to push it further," said Alfonso Prat-Gay, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at JP Morgan in London. \par \par \uc2  Despite a 0.7 percent month-on-month rise in the headline figure in U.S. July retail sales released on Thursday, the statistics were consistent with a view the U.S. economy was slowing down but might need a rate tightening to engineer a soft landing. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the Fed is not seen as being behind the curve, that is not necessarily bad news for the dollar," Prat-Gay said. "Because everything is under control, the Fed is the next one to move and short-run rates going up should support the dollar". \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $1.0631/34 at 1530 GMT, compared with a low of $1.6022 and with $1.0659/64 in late European trading on Wednesday. The dollar was at 1.5060/74 Swiss francs versus a high of 1.5079 and 1.5016/26 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Gay-Prat predicted euro/dollar would be at $1.12 by the end of the year and the dollar would be at 120 yen, assuming there would be a soft landing in the U.S. economy and a partial recovery in Japan. \par \par \uc2  The present dollar rally has enabled Japanese exports to be priced more competitively and helped the Asian economy to expand out of a prolonged trough. \par \par \uc2  The greenback's advance pushed the yen to two-week lows to at 116.04 yen before retracing to 115.78/86 yen at 1537 GMT, versus 115.14/19 in late Wednesday trading. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect further weakening in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aided by further Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We're certainly looking for a weaker yen," \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist Francis Breedon at Lehman Brothers said. "Up until now the Bank of Japan hasn't been aggressive enough in weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There's potential for more weakening". \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities have a good track record in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and would want to maintain that, he added. \par \par \uc2  "We're waiting for a quiet bomb to be set off in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he said. "Historically, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made huge amounts of money out of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars down at 80 yen in the mid-1990s and sold at 140 last year, he said. "With hindsight, they bought at the right level. They could end up winning this." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least seven times since June 10 to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most recently on July 21. \par \par \uc2  Prat-Gay said the Japanese authorities were in a wait-and-see mode, watching the economy and the Nikkei stock index but would not run the risk of seeing the present economic recovery being blown off course by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "The one thing they don't want is to have this tentative recovery being spoiled by things they could have controlled," he said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8c02l6n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
