\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Japan Little Help In Finance Ministry's Fight To Weaken Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nathan Lewis, Staff Reporter \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1999\par 03:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fought to weaken the yen in recent weeks, but it hasn't had much help from the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "There's no link between MOF and BOJ policy," said Warburg Dillon Read's Tokyo economist Brian Rose. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cooperated with the ministry by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets repeatedly, the BOJ has negated the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through sterilization, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sterilized, its effects tend to be diminished," said economist Richard Jerram at ING-Barings in Tokyo. "Unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more effective." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least six times since June 10, selling large amounts of yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Still, the dollar has weakened to around 115 yen from 121 yen at the start of June. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has moved to sterilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by sopping up excess funds in the money market to keep liquidity growth in line with policy objectives. \par \par \uc2  By capping the amount of yen in circulation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps fundamental monetary conditions unchanged, limiting the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a short-lived market disruption, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Sterilization effectively puts a floor under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be sticking to its money market policy - and canceling out the finance ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy - in order to maintain its independence, which was bolstered when the BOJ Law took effect in April 1998. \par \par \uc2  Changing its money market policy to appease the finance ministry "would take power away from the BOJ," said Warburg Dillon Read's Rose. \par \par \uc2  By flooding the market with its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a government or \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be able to push exchange rates as far down as it would like. But despite selling billions of dollars worth of yen in the past two months, the BOJ has worked to keep a lid on liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Since early April 7, the BOJ has kept around 1 trillion to 1.2 trillion yen ($8.74 billion to $10.49 billion) in excess banking reserves in the money market, quickly absorbing yen injected through its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also would effectively ease monetary policy, which the BOJ has rejected on grounds that such a step might trigger inflation. Prices are now moving flat to slightly downward. \par \par \uc2  In past months, the BOJ has come under political pressure to increase the supply of yen to relieve deflationary pressures and help domestic consumption recover. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ clearly stated that it is opposed to any more quantitative easing steps," said Goldman Sachs economist Yoshito Sakakibara. \par \par \uc2  If the yen continues to rise, political pressure may mount for the BOJ and MOF to work out some sort of agreement. \par \par \uc2  "It's probably reasonable to say MOF is hoping the BOJ will undertake unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if sterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fails," Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, there are reports that the BOJ is arguing with MOF about the funding of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying the government should float bonds - in effect using tax money - to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Rose at Warburg Dillon Read noted the BOJ could expand liquidity simply through money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would tend to weaken the yen without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  If \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  really wanted to lower the value of the yen, "it would be more effective to have a genuine change in monetary policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  -Nathan Lewis; (813)5255-2929; nlewis@ap.org \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329dv8503cas\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
