\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Japan Little Help In MOF's Fight To Weaken Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nathan Lewis \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1999\par 02:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fought to weaken the yen in recent weeks, but it hasn't had much help from the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "There's no link between MOF and BOJ policy," said Warburg Dillon Read's Tokyo economist Brian Rose. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cooperated with the ministry by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets repeatedly, the BOJ has negated the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through sterilization, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sterilized, its effects tend to be diminished," said economist Richard Jerram at ING-Barings in Tokyo. "Unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more effective." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least six times since June 10, selling large amounts of yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Still, the dollar has weakened to around Y115 from Y121 at the start of June. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has moved to sterilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by sopping up excess funds in the money market to keep liquidity growth in line with policy objectives. \par \par \uc2  By capping the amount of yen in circulation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps fundamental monetary conditions unchanged, limiting the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a short-lived market disruption, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Sterilization effectively puts a floor under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to be sticking to its money\par market policy - and canceling out the finance ministry's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy\par - in order to maintain its independence, which was bolstered when the\par BOJ Law took effect in April 1998.\par -\par        BOJ Opposed To Further Monetary Easing\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Changing its money market policy to appease the finance ministry\par "would take power away from the BOJ," said Rose.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By flooding the market with its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a government or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par should be able to push exchange rates as far down as it would like. But\par despite selling billions of dollars worth of yen in the past two months,\par the BOJ has worked to keep a lid on liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since early April 7, the BOJ has kept around Y1.0 trillion to Y1.2\par trillion in excess banking reserves in the money market, quickly\par absorbing yen injected through its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Unsterilized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would also effectively ease monetary policy,\par which the BOJ has rejected on grounds that such a step might trigger\par inflation. Prices are now moving flat to slightly downward.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In past months, the BOJ has come under political pressure to increase\par the supply of yen to relieve deflationary pressures and help domestic\par consumption recover.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ clearly stated that it is opposed to any more quantitative\par easing steps," said Goldman Sachs economist Yoshito Sakakibara.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the yen continues to rise, political pressure may mount for the BOJ\par and MOF to work out some sort of agreement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's probably reasonable to say MOF is hoping the BOJ will undertake\par unsterilized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if sterilized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fails," Sakakibara\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, there are reports that the BOJ is arguing with MOF about\par the funding of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying the government should float bonds -\par in effect using tax money - to finance \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rose at Warburg Dillon Read noted the BOJ could expand liquidity\par simply through money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which would tend to weaken the\par yen without \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  really wanted to lower the value of the yen, "it would be\par more effective to have a genuine change in monetary policy," he said.\par    -Nathan Lewis; (813)5255-2929; nlewis@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-08-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0003GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8505v4k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
