\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Euro Heavy Vs Dlr; Consolidating Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1999\par 02:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  While the impact of Summers' remarks was limited, comments from Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  international bureau head Zembei Mizoguchi had no discernible effect whatsoever. Mizoguchi said Japan would take proper steps against yen strength, but his refusal to specifically comment on joint U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was taken as another sign that such action is unlikely. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa hinted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could happen below Y115.00, and the fact that it did not "makes us less responsive to what he says," a Tokyo trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  With official remarks - or lack thereof - raining on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fire, dealers wonder exactly what rekindle the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's spark. \par \par \uc2  "We think that if (the BOJ) comes into the market, they would do so in the middle of a short covering rally like what happened on Tuesday," when MOF released its rare statement saying that Summers and Miyazawa had chatted on the phone about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, the city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the dollar had already been rising in the wake of its overnight plunge below Y114.00, so the statement had maximum market impact, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, is assessed as top-heavy after its recent rapid recovery. However, a fall below support at $1.0700 isn't expected in Asian session, dealers said. Against the yen, the euro is seen consolidating in the Y122.50-Y123.50 range, taking cues mainly from dollar-yen moves, they said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was trading at Y123.22, down from Y123.29 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was quoted late in Tokyo Wednesday at Y123.46. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6203, down from $1.6217 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6210 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite; 813-5255-2929; ltwaronite@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0049GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8505v9s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
