\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Dollar Seen Capped Around Y115.00 \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1999\par 03:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  While the dollar rose to Y114.84 earlier, many Tokyo traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces heavy resistance around Y115.00 on offers chiefly from U.S. funds. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. funds will actively sell the dollar when the dollar/yen drifts higher above Y115.00," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, who heads the International Bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reiterated Tuesday morning that Japan is in contact with other nations on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. He added that Japan's policy hadn't changed. \par \par \uc2  Finance minister Kiichi Miyazawa responded to a question at a press conference by denying the impossibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Miyazawa also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. have sustained close contact. \par \par \uc2  Trade minister Kaoru Yosano said that the yen's recent rise reflected the weakness of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yosano also said the Bank of Japan needed to watch the yen's moves carefully. \par \par \uc2  "While government officials warned against the yen's recent strengthening, the impact on the dollar-yen was limited. Market attention is fixed on U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," a senior trader at a Japanese trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  The euro edged higher to Y122.63 in tandem with the dollar-yen rally in the Asian morning. \par \par \uc2  "The euro-yen rally was due to bullish moves in the dollar-yen Tuesday morning. With a lack of leads for the euro-yen, it will follow the dollar-yen's moves throughout the Asian session, said a senior trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was trading at Y122.28, slightly down from Y122.33 in New York late Monday. The euro was quoted late in Tokyo Monday at Y121.78. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6165, down from $1.6177 in New York late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen trading between Y113.95-Y115.00, while the euro is expected to trade between $1.0660-$1.0690 for the rest of the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  -By Hidenobu Kageyama; 813-5255-2929; hkageyama@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0121GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8305oad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
