\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW: Yoshitomi -3: After Yen Rise Vs Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1999\par 08:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "High interest rates would choke off residential construction and business investment, while the strong yen would have a negative impact on Japan's nascent economic recovery," Yoshitomi said. \par \par \uc2  "This is why the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been engaging in smoothing out \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)," he added. \par \par \uc2  In the last two months, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets several times on behalf of the finance ministry to curb the yen's strengthening, but the yen has continued to soar against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the yen's sharp rise versus the dollar, Yoshitomi said, "For Japanese manufacturers, the equilibrium (breakeven) range is Y110-115, given their international competitiveness." \par \par \uc2  But, he said a higher range for dollar-yen would be desirable, saying, "Y120-125 is the appropriate range for dollar-yen, given the difference in business cycles between the U.S. and Japan and the equilibrium range for Japanese manufacturers." \par \par \uc2  At 0600 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y115.52, and the euro was trading at Y123.15. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0610GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8305ox0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
