\par\par \b \uc2  Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy unchanged-MOF's Mizoguchi. \b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1999\par 02:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 3 (Reuters) - Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (MOF) International Bureau, said on Tuesday that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "Our thinking has not changed," Mizoguchi told reporters when asked about the yen's continued rise against the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have repeatedly said they are ready to take decisive action to prevent a premature yen rise, but \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent days despite the yen's rise to 5-month highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Japanese authorities were still prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizoguchi said, "I cannot say specifically what we will or won't do." \par \par \uc2  Asked if Japan was in close contact with other nations' authorities on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, "We are (in contact) as needed." Asked if that included U.S. authorities, he said, "Generally speaking, we always are." ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8303fb8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
